WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.200 --> 00:00:03.080
I believe it is the
artist's responsibility

00:00:03.080 --> 00:00:05.060
to lead people into hell.

00:00:07.880 --> 00:00:13.170
But I also believe it's
important to lead the way out.

00:00:13.170 --> 00:00:15.630
We are in a renaissance
of documentary.

00:00:15.630 --> 00:00:19.070
People are realizing that there
is as much drama in what is

00:00:19.070 --> 00:00:23.030
and what was as anything that
the human imagination dreams up.

00:00:26.830 --> 00:00:30.205
And you have the added
advantage of it being true.

00:00:33.000 --> 00:00:34.960
In order to be a
good director, you

00:00:34.960 --> 00:00:38.370
have to be able to
tolerate contradiction.

00:00:38.370 --> 00:00:40.670
There's no objective truth.

00:00:40.670 --> 00:00:42.110
This is human experience.

00:00:42.110 --> 00:00:44.797
We see things from
different perspectives.

00:00:44.797 --> 00:00:47.600
And that's OK.

00:00:47.600 --> 00:00:50.130
It's really important
that history not be

00:00:50.130 --> 00:00:53.460
distilled to sort of
the Great Men theory.

00:00:53.460 --> 00:00:55.470
All of those people
that are famous

00:00:55.470 --> 00:00:57.480
don't do the fighting
and the dying.

00:00:57.480 --> 00:01:01.825
The best history is the place
where so-called ordinary people

00:01:01.825 --> 00:01:02.325
exist.

00:01:06.940 --> 00:01:09.840
You want to use everything
at your disposal

00:01:09.840 --> 00:01:12.930
to activate your
audience's imagination.

00:01:12.930 --> 00:01:14.790
[PUNCHES LANDING]

00:01:14.790 --> 00:01:15.816
The cannon firing.

00:01:15.816 --> 00:01:16.440
[CANNON FIRING]

00:01:16.440 --> 00:01:17.760
Troops tramping.

00:01:17.760 --> 00:01:18.261
Bat cracking

00:01:19.580 --> 00:01:21.807
There are millions
things that you

00:01:21.807 --> 00:01:23.890
can do-- that you have to
do-- until you go, whoa.

00:01:23.890 --> 00:01:24.556
That's working.

00:01:32.580 --> 00:01:34.950
We find ourselves in one of
the most challenging moments

00:01:34.950 --> 00:01:36.510
in the history of
the United States.

00:01:36.510 --> 00:01:40.770
The role of the filmmaker then
becomes even more important

00:01:40.770 --> 00:01:43.020
and more urgent.

00:01:43.020 --> 00:01:46.230
If you've got that thing that
is burning inside you saying,

00:01:46.230 --> 00:01:49.680
I have to do this.

00:01:49.680 --> 00:01:52.920
Now we can begin to talk
about how you start.

00:01:52.920 --> 00:01:57.140
I'm Ken Burns, and this
is my MasterClass.

